<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Aurunci</h1><p class="st-meta">700 BCE – 314 BCE (approx.) · capital Suessa Aurunca</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Ancient Italic people of the coast between Latium and Campania, whose towns were destroyed by Rome in 314 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Aurunci, called Ausones by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a>, lived between the Liri and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volturno">Volturno</a> rivers around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roccamonfina">Roccamonfina</a> volcano. Greek writers used 'Ausonia' for much of early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, which suggests they were once a widespread people. Little is known of their origins or language.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Known only from Roman and Greek sources, the Aurunci lived in hill towns such as Ausona, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minturnae">Minturnae</a>, Vescia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suessa-aurunca">Suessa Aurunca</a>. They fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latins</a> in the late 6th and early 5th centuries BCE, and in the 4th century came under Roman protection; in 337 BCE, under attack from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sidicini">Sidicini</a>, they abandoned their town of Aurunca for Suessa.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After they joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome's</a> enemies during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samnite-wars">Samnite Wars</a>, Rome destroyed the towns of Ausona, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minturnae">Minturnae</a> and Vescia in 314 BCE, massacring much of the population. Roman colonies followed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suessa-aurunca">Suessa Aurunca</a> in 313 BCE and Minturnae in 296 BCE, and the people disappeared from history.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/aurunci.jpg" alt="Aurunci" width="320" height="242"><figcaption>Image: ColdEel &amp;amp; Ahenobarbus · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carte_GuerreRomanoAurunce_345avJC.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>700 BCE – 314 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Suessa Aurunca</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ausones</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-507&amp;focus=aurunci" aria-label="Aurunci on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5020 707 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Aurunci lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5340 963L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5340 963h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5340 963h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Suessa Aurunca. <a href="/atlas?year=-507&amp;focus=aurunci">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

